{#
  MiddleTruncation macro -- a string shortened in the middle to fit its width, keeping the start and the end.

  A server cannot measure a width, so the macro renders the markup contract and nothing more: the full text twice, once
  in .middle-truncation-visual (aria-hidden) and once in .middle-truncation-full (which the consumer's CSS visually hides),
  with the options as data attributes. Measuring and shortening happen in the browser: add the script from
  html-headless's middle-truncation.html (it reads these data attributes), or use the Web Components element. Without
  either, the full text is shown. To shorten on the server, pass params.shortened (computed with shared/middle-truncation.ts
  and a character-count measure, for example).

  HTML tag: <span> holding two <span>s
  CSS class: middle-truncation (sub-elements: middle-truncation-visual, middle-truncation-full)
  Accessibility:
    - the shortened text is aria-hidden; the full text is what assistive technology, find-in-page and copy receive.
    - the consumer's CSS bounds the root (display: block; overflow: hidden; white-space: nowrap) and visually hides
      .middle-truncation-full (clipped, never display: none).

  Params:
    text        string   Required. The full text (escaped).
    ellipsis    string   Required, no default. The cut marker.
    strategy    string   "even" (default) | "fixed-end" | "min-end".
    end         number   Characters kept at the end for "fixed-end" and "min-end".
    shortened   string   Optional, already shortened text for the visual span (sets data-truncated).
    id          string   Element id.
    classes     string   Consumer-provided extra CSS classes.
    attributes  object   Extra HTML attributes as key/value pairs.

  Usage:
    {% from "components/middle-truncation/macro.njk" import middleTruncation %}
    {{ middleTruncation({ text: "quarterly-report-final-version-3.pdf", ellipsis: "…", strategy: "min-end", end: 6 }) }}
#}
{%- macro middleTruncation(params) -%}
{%- set p = params | default({}) -%}
{%- set strategy = p.strategy or "even" -%}
<span
  class="middle-truncation{% if p.classes %} {{ p.classes }}{% endif %}"
  data-strategy="{{ strategy }}"
  data-ellipsis="{{ p.ellipsis }}"
  {%- if p.end is defined and p.end !== none %} data-end="{{ p.end }}"{% endif %}
  {%- if p.shortened %} data-truncated{% endif %}
  {%- if p.id %} id="{{ p.id }}"{% endif %}
  {%- if p.attributes %}{% for k, v in p.attributes %} {{ k }}="{{ v }}"{% endfor %}{% endif %}
><span class="middle-truncation-visual" aria-hidden="true">{{ p.shortened or p.text }}</span><span class="middle-truncation-full">{{ p.text }}</span></span>
{%- endmacro -%}
